    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d748">

                <pb facs="0888" n="792" sameAs="frus:frus1921v02/pg792"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">361.11/3697: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Czechoslovakia</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Crane</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Prague</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-03-30T17:00:00+01:00"><hi rendition="#italic">March 30,
                                1921—5 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 10:36
                    p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>27. Your telegram number 17, February 28, 7 p.m.<anchor n="95" xml:id="d748-f1"/>
                    The Foreign Office has learned that the attitude of the Soviets would be that
                    the United States must treat with them directly on the question and <pb
                        facs="0889" n="793" xml:id="pg793"/> that the Americans are held more or
                    less as hostages. The Czechs will continue their efforts but I do not expect
                    success. There are no new names to report.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Crane</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
